## Keep a diary

Note what you eat, how you feel and your symptoms for a few weeks. It can help you and your GP spot triggers.

## Eating habits

- eat slowly and regularly
- drink plenty of water
- try not to cut out whole food groups without advice

## Stress

The gut and brain are closely linked. Relaxation, exercise, mindfulness and good sleep can all help.

## Exercise

Regular activity, such as walking, yoga or swimming, can ease symptoms, especially constipation and bloating.

## Toilet access

- a **Radar key** opens thousands of locked accessible toilets. See [accessible toilets](/support/leisure/accessible-toilets/)
- a **"Can't Wait" card** from Crohn's and Colitis UK or Bladder and Bowel UK can help you ask to use a toilet in shops and cafes

## Support

**The IBS Network** is a UK charity with a helpline, self-care plan and a "Can't Wait" card for members.
